  "reference_protocol": "Every complete SQL statement is put on a separate input line, preserving its SQL text; the same formatted SQL is sent to both drivers. sqlite3 -bail can still execute later statements on the same line after an ALTER runtime error. The retained raw-line stage exhibited that difference. Python sqlite3.complete_statement is used only by the comparison harness as a lexical statement boundary helper, never by the Lean runtime.",
  "snapshot_protocol": "Catalog, rowids, rows and integrity-check return code/stdout/stderr are compared. Existing invalid CHECK programs can make integrity_check itself fail; those diagnostics remain observed data.",
