    "The 88-case feature sample retains 22 failures and is not a compatibility percentage.",
    "The row-check theorem is a component success contract, not whole-SQL equivalence, physical ALTER refinement or a crash proof. The source-aware ADD trace premises now refer to executeBase, which includes the constraint scan.",
    "A new CHECK triggers a scan of old and new clauses. Adding a plain column retains SQLite behavior and does not request this scan. Empty tables do not evaluate CHECK predicates.",
    "ignore_check_constraints, generated/STRICT columns and other existing SQL/schema/storage limitations remain. The 60 SIGKILL cases cover earlier storage paths, not all ALTER crash stages."
